{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-chain-ring-comparison-table3-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:chain-ring-comparison-table3-data","kind":"table","title":"Table 3 from prop:chain-ring-comparison","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-chain-ring-comparison"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"chain-ring-comparison-table3-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"tbl:chain-ring-comparison-table3-data\"></a>\n<strong>Table.</strong> <em>Table 3 from prop:chain-ring-comparison</em></p>\n<p>For each carbocyclic ring, the table records the ring size <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N</code> alongside the torus-link delta <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_{T(2,N)}</code> evaluated at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\approx 1</code>, the associated open-chain weight, and the molecular energy ratio <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta E / \\lvert q+q^{-1}\\rvert_{\\mathrm{mol}}</code>, so the ring-vs-chain comparison can be read off at a glance. The benzene row (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N = 6</code>) is set in bold.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Ring</th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N</code></th>\n<th align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_{T(2,N)}(q \\approx 1)</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\">Chain weight</th>\n<th align=\"right\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta E / \\lvert q+q^{-1}\\rvert_{\\mathrm{mol}}</code></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Cyclobutadiene</td>\n<td align=\"center\">4</td>\n<td align=\"right\">2</td>\n<td align=\"center\">3</td>\n<td align=\"right\">1</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Benzene</strong></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><strong>6</strong></td>\n<td align=\"right\"><strong>3</strong></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><strong>5</strong></td>\n<td align=\"right\"><strong>2</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cyclooctatetraene</td>\n<td align=\"center\">8</td>\n<td align=\"right\">4</td>\n<td align=\"center\">7</td>\n<td align=\"right\">3</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Cyclodecane</td>\n<td align=\"center\">10</td>\n<td align=\"right\">5</td>\n<td align=\"center\">9</td>\n<td align=\"right\">4</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"}
